- given that an API is having latency, how would you optimise it.
solution:
1. API profiling(DB query, Network I/O, CPU Utilisation, compute)
2. Data Optimizations
    •	Cache frequently accessed data (Redis, in-memory).
    •	Use pagination or projections to fetch only required fields.
    •	Optimize DB queries and add appropriate indexes.
3.	Code-Level Improvements
    •	Avoid blocking I/O by using async or non-blocking calls (e.g., CompletableFuture, Reactor).
    •	Use connection pooling and efficient serialization (e.g., JSON → Protobuf if large payloads).
    •	Batch or debounce requests when possible.
4.	Infrastructure & Network
	•	Reduce hops between services; consider co-locating dependent services.
	•	Enable HTTP/2, compression, and persistent connections.
	•	Scale horizontally and load balancing
	•	add a CDN for static content.
5.	Architectural Changes (if systemic)
	•	Introduce caching layers, rate limiters, or message queues for load leveling.
	•	Break large synchronous chains into event-driven or asynchronous pipelines.
